CORE
main.cpp
--pointer-check --validate-goto-model
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ initialized once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ initializer uses this: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A block-scope static whose initializer is not a constant expression kept
that initializer as its symbol value, so __CPROVER_initialize evaluated it
at program start, before any call: with undefined parameters and `this'.
This was the remaining failure of std::regex_match (libstdc++'s
_AnyMatcher::operator(), `static auto __nul = _M_translator._M_translate(0)').
